Missing PC connectivity or pairing disables affected remote operations only; it must not disable otherwise authorized local work. Network-dependent provider/authentication operations remain subject to their real availability and access rules. Local LCL validation must not secretly require a Desktop service.", "C20 — Installed Desktop Application Contract
Desktop Nexees must be an installed, locally running application with its own window, local workspace/files, terminal integration and local agent runtime. A browser tab, PWA-only delivery, or hosted website displayed in an application window does not satisfy the Desktop requirement. Core local workspace operation must not depend on a hosted UI website.

**OPEN DECISION DESKTOP-RENDERER-01:** the user has not yet clarified whether an Electron-style installed desktop application is acceptable or all Electron/Chromium/WebView rendering is prohibited. Do not silently select either interpretation. TASK-003 must obtain that decision before approving a renderer-dependent foundation; TASK-009 must use the approved choice. Requirements/documentation and unrelated feasibility research may continue, but do not implement a conflicting shell or claim this decision resolved.", "C21 — Execution Host and Revision Contract
An agent is bound to an execution device, workspace/checkout and approved specification revision as well as its model. UI focus, provider switching, connectivity changes and synchronization do not implicitly transfer that authority. Handoff requires an acknowledged safe checkpoint and compatible destination capabilities. Unreachable-host failover must not create duplicate authoritative executors.", "C22 — Safe Content Reconciliation Contract
Synchronize selected content and portable state with revision-aware conflicts, crash-safe application and no secret/permission replication. Remote commands and approvals are authenticated control messages, not ordinary offline sync records. Do not replay stale actions or replace unsaved source/LCL changes silently. New LCL revisions require validation and explicit adoption at a safe boundary before changing a running agent's constraints.", "C23 — LCL Import Contract
Desktop and independent Android accept individual/multiple LCL files and ZIP packages. `architecture/lcl_import_pipeline.lcl.txt` defines bounded staging, semantics-preserving structure planning, conflict-safe preview/commit and separate validated adoption. Import has no ambient execution authority.", "C24 — Model Orientation Contract
Changing a supported provider/model mid-session preserves progress and invokes the default-ON read-only orientation in `architecture/model_handoff.lcl.txt`. Users can enable/disable that extra phase; identity, authoritative state, tool scope, approval and security checks always remain. The model may continue automatically after successful orientation within the existing autonomy permissions.", "C25 — Human-Readable Code and Cleanup Contract
`policies/code_readability_and_cleanup.lcl.txt` is a completion requirement on every implementation task. Readability/comment review, task-owned cleanup and final-revision verification evidence are mandatory; unknown files and user changes are protected.", "C26 — Dual Manual Contract
`architecture/manuals_and_help.lcl.txt` requires separate release-matched Nexees and integrated-LCL manuals on Desktop and Android, including offline access, tested examples, navigation/search and coverage of all approved modes.", "C27 — Implementation Root and Repository Contract
For TASK-001 through TASK-075, the development working directory is `/mnt/F/Nexees/` and repository identity is `https://github.com/aivars11232/Nexees`. B26 in `bindings/bindings.lcl.txt` defines the mandatory local identity check, approved URL equivalents, preservation and stop behavior. Each task and new implementation-agent session must retain this binding and record its preflight before any source mutation. The URL alone grants no Git write or publication permission. Product workspace roots remain independently selected and scoped; Android does not inherit this PC path.", "C28 — Bidirectional Device Control
Both Desktop and Android can send and, when separately enabled, receive supported typed requests. Enforce RC-01–RC-26 and the RC-T acceptance scenarios with the assigned task owners.", "C29 — Independent Receiver
Desktop service can remain available while the window is closed, with explicit startup/lifetime settings. Android availability follows its actual OS/session state. No constant LLM inference is needed merely to listen.", "C30 — Destination Authority
Directional per-device grants, explicit device/user/session/workspace targets, receiver-side checks, expiry, replay protection, lock policy, revocation and exact outcome reconciliation are mandatory.", "C31 — App Launch Is Not Whole-Device Control
Permit only supported allowlisted applications/actions. Launch Nexees or HopToDesk safely; do not infer unattended screen/input control, Android unrestricted UI automation or permission bypass.", "Document scope
